&HEAD CHID='geom_hvac_supply_3d_stair', TITLE='Complex Geometry: supply box turned 60 degrees about the axis (-1,1,1), stair-stepped OBST.' /

# Room 10 m x 10 m x 6 m with 0.2 m cells. A box 3.0 m x 2.4 m x 0.4 m (centre 7.1, 5.0, 2.0 m) blows air
# through its small -x face of its own frame: 5 m3/s through 0.96 m2. The air leaves through an open vent in the y=10 m wall.
# Stair-stepped OBST version of the box turned by 60 degrees about the axis (-1,1,1): the 359 grid cells whose center lies in the turned box are OBSTs, and the exposed faces nearest to the supply plane of the box blow (1.48 m2, same 5 m3/s).
# Line devices measure the time-averaged velocity (t > 10 s) on three planes 0.5, 1 and 2 m from the center of the supply
# face, normal to the face; the lines are 5 m long along the long side of the face, in four rows 0.2 m apart (rows -0.3 to 0.3 m
# along the short side). Utilities/Python/scripts/geom_hvac_supply_jet.py reads the file geom_hvac_supply_3d_stair_line.csv.
&MESH ID='Mesh01', IJK=50,50,30, XB=0.0,10.0,0.0,10.0,0.0,6.0 /
&TIME T_END=30. /
&MISC RND_SEED=101 /
&DUMP DT_DEVC=0.1, DT_SLCF=1. /
&PRES SOLVER='UGLMAT' /

&SURF ID='SUPPLY', VEL=-3.378378, COLOR='BLUE' /

&OBST XB=5.2,5.4,5.0,5.2,2.4,2.6, SURF_ID6='INERT','INERT','SUPPLY','INERT','INERT','SUPPLY' /
&OBST XB=5.4,5.6,5.0,5.2,2.4,2.6, SURF_ID6='INERT','INERT','INERT','INERT','INERT','INERT' /
